    {
      "id": "q30",
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "Evaluate $\\sqrt{1-10a+25a^2}-4a$ at $a=15.2$ and $4x-\\sqrt{1+6x+9x^2}$ at $x=3.18$. Choose the complete calculation pair.",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "A",
            "text": "$|5a-1|-4a=(1-5a)-4a=-135.8$; $4x-|3x+1|=4x+(3x+1)=23.26$.",
            "figure_ids": []
          },
          {
            "id": "B",
            "text": "$|5a-1|-4a=5a-1=75$; $4x-|3x+1|=-(3x+1)=-10.54$.",
            "figure_ids": []
          },
          {
            "id": "C",
            "text": "$|5a-1|-4a=(5a-1)-4a=a-1=14.2$; $4x-|3x+1|=4x-(3x+1)=x-1=2.18$.",
            "figure_ids": []
          },
          {
            "id": "D",
            "text": "$|5a-1|-4a=(5a-1)-4a=a-1=14.2$; $4x-|3x+1|=4x-3x+1=x+1=4.18$.",
            "figure_ids": []
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q31",
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "For every real $x>5$, let $E=\\left(\\frac{x+5}{x^2-5x}-\\frac{x}{x^2-25}\\right)\\frac{x^2-25}{5}$. Which argument proves $2<E<3$ for every such $x$?",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "A",
            "text": "After factoring, $E=2+5/x$. Since $x>5$, $5/x>1$, so $E>3$.",
            "figure_ids": []
          },
          {
            "id": "B",
            "text": "For $x=10$, $E=2.5$ and $2<2.5<3$. This proves the bound for every $x>5$.",
            "figure_ids": []
          },
          {
            "id": "C",
            "text": "Factoring gives $E=2+5/x$. Since $x>5$, $5/x>0$, so $E>2$. This establishes both requested bounds.",
            "figure_ids": []
          },
          {
            "id": "D",
            "text": "The denominators are nonzero. Factoring gives $E=(x+5)^2/(5x)-x/5=2+5/x$. Since $x>5$, $0<5/x<1$, hence $2<E<3$.",
            "figure_ids": []
          }
        ]
      }
    }
